# Git Workflow

## Branching

- Create a dedicated branch for every feature or bugfix.
- Always branch from an up-to-date `main`.
- Naming:
  - Features: `feat/<short-description>`
  - Bugfixes: `fix/<short-description>`
- Examples: `feat/espnow-debounce`, `fix/display-flicker`

## Starting work

1. `git checkout main`
2. `git pull origin main`
3. `git checkout -b feat/<name>` or `git checkout -b fix/<name>`

## During work

- Keep commits focused and use conventional commit messages (`feat`, `fix`, `chore`, `docs`, `refactor`, `test`).
- Do not commit secrets or local-only files.
- Only commit when explicitly asked.

## Finishing work

1. Ensure the feature or bugfix is complete and tested as needed.
2. Update `main` if needed: `git checkout main` then `git pull origin main`.
3. Merge the branch into `main` locally (fast-forward preferred when possible).
4. Push `main` only when explicitly asked.
5. Delete the local feature/fix branch after a successful merge.

## Do not

- Do not create pull requests or merge requests for this project.
- Do not open branches from anything other than `main`.
- Do not push feature/fix branches unless explicitly asked.
